      en: "The National Museum of Montenegro (Narodni muzej Crne Gore) is located in Cetinje, the historic capital of Montenegro. Founded in 1896, the museum comprises several departments, including the Historical Museum, the Art Museum, and the Ethnographic Museum. It is housed in the former royal palace of King Nikola I. The collections include over 100,000 objects, including archaeological finds, weapons, coins, paintings, and folk art. The museum documents the history of Montenegro from antiquity to the present. It is an important cultural center and one of the most significant museums in the Balkans. The building itself is a 19th-century architectural monument.",
