      en: "The Royal Palace in Cetinje, built in 1867, served as the residence of King Nikola I Petrović-Njegoš. The historicist architecture blends neoclassical and romantic styles. The palace includes a throne room, library, and private chambers. Today it houses the National Museum of Montenegro, displaying weapons, orders, and historical documents. The Kingdom of Montenegro was proclaimed here in 1910. The palace park is open to the public. It remains a symbol of Montenegrin statehood and a key cultural institution.",
