      en: "Vladika Palace in Cetinje, built in the 19th century, served as the residence of Montenegrin metropolitan bishops. This neoclassical building now houses the Museum of Montenegrin History, displaying weapons, coins, and manuscripts. Located in the city center near Cetinje Monastery, the palace features original period furniture. It represents the fusion of religious and political power in Montenegro's history. The palace is a key cultural institution and a popular tourist attraction.",
